---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import ClaimLabel from "../components/ClaimLabel.astro";
import StatusBadge from "../components/StatusBadge.astro";
import NewsletterForm from "../components/NewsletterForm.astro";
import { CLAIMS, STATUS, type ClaimKind, type RobotStatus } from "../lib/format";
const ld = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "AboutPage",
  name: "About ShinyMetal",
  url: "https://shinymetal.bot/about",
  description: "How ShinyMetal labels claims, sources stories and stays independent.",
};
---
<Base title="About and how we label claims" description="ShinyMetal is an independent publication about home and humanoid robots. We label every claim shipped, preorder, promise, rumor or research, and we never sell robots." jsonLd={ld}>
  <div class="page-head">
    <span class="fd-eyebrow">About</span>
    <h1>The owner's manual for the robot age</h1>
    <p>ShinyMetal follows the robots that are heading for your home: what they can do, what they cost, and whether the company behind them keeps its word.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="prose-page">
    <p>Almost nobody owns a home humanoid yet. Companies are announcing, demoing and taking deposits, and the news is a mix of real progress, careful marketing and rumor. We sort it. Every story and every spec carries a label that says how sure anyone can be.</p>

    <h2 id="labels">How we label claims</h2>
    <p>The word is the signal. The color and glyph only confirm it, so the label reads the same in print and for readers who don't see color.</p>
  </div>
  <ul class="legend" style="margin:var(--space-4) 0 var(--space-6)">
    {(Object.keys(CLAIMS) as ClaimKind[]).map((k) => <li><span><ClaimLabel kind={k} /></span><span>{CLAIMS[k].help}</span></li>)}
  </ul>
  <div class="prose-page">
    <p>Rumors also carry a confidence rating from 0 to 100. We explain the number in the story: who reported it, how many independent sources agree, and what would confirm it.</p>

    <h2 id="status">Robot status</h2>
    <p>Each robot in the <a href="/robots">database</a> has one status, backed by a dated source in the <a href="/tracker">reality tracker</a>.</p>
  </div>
  <ul class="legend" style="margin:var(--space-4) 0 var(--space-6)">
    {(Object.keys(STATUS) as RobotStatus[]).map((k) => <li><span><StatusBadge status={k} /></span><span>{STATUS[k].help}</span></li>)}
  </ul>
  <div class="prose-page">
    <h2 id="legal">The legal layer</h2>
    <p>For each robot we note whether it holds US FCC equipment authorization. On 28 July 2026 the FCC added foreign-made mobile robots over 2 kg (4.4 lb) to its Covered List, so new models from outside the US can't be authorized. Models approved before that date can still be sold. We also note known security flaws, and whether a remote human operator can drive the robot inside your home. A dash or "unknown" means the maker hasn't said and we couldn't verify it.</p>

    <h2 id="promises">The promise ledger</h2>
    <p>When a company says something will happen by a date, we log it with the source. When the date arrives we mark it kept, slipped or broken, and we link what actually happened. The <a href="/promises">ledger</a> is the long memory the robot industry doesn't keep for itself.</p>

    <h2 id="sources">Sources and corrections</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Every story lists its sources at the end. We link to primary sources (company releases, papers, filings) wherever they exist.</li>
      <li>We quote companies exactly and decode the quote in plain words underneath.</li>
      <li>Some drafting is assisted by AI research agents. Every fact must carry a source link before it publishes.</li>
      <li>Generated images are labeled as illustrations in their captions. We never present a generated image as a photo of a real product.</li>
      <li>Found a mistake? Email <a href="mailto:tips@shinymetal.bot">tips@shinymetal.bot</a>. We fix errors and note the correction.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="independence">Independence</h2>
    <p>We don't sell robots, and no maker pays for coverage. When we later add affiliate links or sponsors, the disclosure will sit next to the link, not in a footer.</p>

    <h2 id="coming">What's coming</h2>
    <p>Member profiles with a fleet (wishlist to delivered), a reservation queue tracker, a community, a workshop for designs and mods, and deals. Subscribe to hear when each opens.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="margin-top:var(--space-7)"><NewsletterForm source="about" /></div>
</Base>
